Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:18:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Freshwater budget by region; [sea_ice]
 ice_consolidation_thickness and a four-month test at 0.5 m
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

analysis/freshwater_budget.jl: for the regions of salinity_drift.jl and rivers.md, the daily
freshwater content (relative to 34.8, full depth), the fresh water exchanged between regions
across their faces, the surface input as the residual, and the sea-ice volume change; monthly
table, whole-run exchange table, cumulative figure. Why: narrowing the river footprint
(patch 099) left the basins salty and the shelves fresh: is the shelf-to-basin export too weak?

panarctic.jl: [sea_ice] ice_consolidation_thickness (ClimaSeaIce's hᶜ, default 0.05 m, the
earlier behaviour). hᶜ is both Hibler's lead-closing thickness and the consolidation threshold.
config_sep2005_4mo_nemo_glorys12_nz100_hc05.toml: four months with hᶜ = 0.5 m.

analysis/rivers.jl: the routing line says equal shares or depth-weighted shares according to the
NumericalEarth version in use (the 061 worktree is on 0.9.2: equal shares).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
